@startuml FrostProtection
!include theme.puml

' File-local: the theme has no activity colours, so stock PlantUML draws light
' activity boxes and diamonds under the theme's white text. Same fix
' HeatingControlLogic.puml uses.
skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #4682B4
    BorderColor #ffffff
    FontColor #ffffff
    DiamondBackgroundColor #36648B
    DiamondBorderColor #ffffff
    DiamondFontColor #ffffff
}

title Frost Protection - Two Independent Latches\nFlow or room protects the house; tank charges the cylinder

start

:Readings from the sensor set\n(flow, room, tank);

:Mark each reading USABLE = valid AND fresh\n(per reading, independently);
note right
  PER READING, not a single gate on all three. A stale tank
  does not disable room-based protection - only the tank's
  own trigger. Freshness uses per-source timestamps:
  lastBoilerTempUpdateTimestamp for flow and tank,
  insideTempGoodMs for the room.

  Staleness is a trigger condition, not a detail. Nothing
  clears isBoilerTempOutputValid when MB8ART reads STOP, so
  a dead bus left the last value flagged valid forever - a
  frozen warm reading meant frost could never fire again,
  and a frozen cold one would have fired forever.

  An unusable reading can never TRIGGER. On RELEASE it
  counts as "not blocking", so a burn stops rather than
  continuing blind.
end note

if (Any usable reading below 5.0 °C?) then (no)
  if (Latched and every watched reading clear of 10.0 °C?) then (yes)
    :Release the latch;
    stop
  else (no)
    :Hold current state;
    stop
  endif
else (yes)
endif

fork
  :flow OR room cold\n-> heatDemand();
  :Space heating demand\nOVERRIDES heating_enabled;
fork again
  :tank cold\n-> waterDemand();
  :DHW CHARGE\nOVERRIDES water_enabled;
  note right
    The tank used to ask for SPACE heating, which
    warms the house and does nothing for the tank.
  end note
end fork

:Latched until the release threshold;

stop

floating note right
  Thresholds (FrostProtectionPolicy.h):
    TRIGGER_TENTHS = 50   (5.0 °C)
    RELEASE_TENTHS = 100  (10.0 °C)
  Latching, with a static_assert that release is
  above trigger.

  The two latches are INDEPENDENT:
    heatDemand()  watches flow OR room -> space heating
    waterDemand() watches tank         -> DHW charge

  NEITHER overrides boiler_enabled. A drained-for-service
  system is a likely reason to switch the boiler off, and
  firing into a drained boiler is worse than frost.

  Source: include/modules/control/FrostProtectionPolicy.h
          include/modules/control/FrostProtection.h
          src/modules/control/FrostProtection.cpp
  Shipped in 9bf6be5. Demand side: HeatingControlLogic.puml.
end note

@enduml
